    "done_when": "settings.py owns eddb_host, set by --eddb-host or IMAS_ALAMBIC_EDDB_HOST: unset keeps the ssh route to jt-60sa, a host name composes the ssh route to that host through one function in eddb_remote.py that keeps -F ~/.ssh/config and the remote module-load shell (DEFAULT_SSH_COMMAND becomes that function applied to jt-60sa), and the value local gives an empty ssh_command with remote_python=sys.executable; imas-alambic config prints eddb_host with its source. write builds the channel requests its signal maps declare for each pulse and passes them to eddb.fetch_channels before writing, so a cached pulse makes no transport call and refused channels stay in the receipt. install/imasdb.sh launcher exports IMAS_ALAMBIC_EDDB_HOST=local beside IMAS_ALAMBIC_HOME. In the new packages/imas-alambic/tests/test_write_fetch.py, against a synthetic flat bundle and eddb_standin.py over the local transport, write on pulse 900001 with no cache fetches its mapped channels and writes ids/900001_0.nc, a second write with overwrite makes no transport call, and a refused channel is reported without stopping the write. test_settings.py pins eddb_host: flag beats variable, unset keeps the jt-60sa ssh route, local gives the local transport with sys.executable, and the composed ssh command for a host keeps -F ~/.ssh/config and the module-load shell. packages/imas-alambic/tests adds no failures against the base, judged by failure ids from one base run and one head run, each logged once. uv run --no-sync ruff check imas_ambix tests packages exits 0. All runs on the fleet allocation in place.",
